        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f521ef62-6749-5ca2-82ba-50a5cf932cc7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Amélie Mauresmo, Pam Shriver, Loïc Courteau, Betsy Nagelsen\n- Events: 1985 Edgbaston Cup – Singles\n- Roles: tennis player, coach, doubles specialist, world No. 1\n\nFacts:\n- Pam Shriver was the defending champion of the 1985 Edgbaston Cup – Singles and won the final against Betsy Nagelsen 6–1, 6–0.\n- Loïc Courteau has coached the French Fed Cup team in the past.\n- Since 2002, Loïc Courteau has been the coach of Amélie Mauresmo.\n- Amélie Mauresmo was born on 5 July 1979 and is a French former professional tennis player and former world No. 1.\n- Pam Shriver was born on July 4, 1962 and is an American former professional tennis player known primarily as a doubles specialist, with success also in singles.\n- Amélie Mauresmo won two Grand Slam titles.",
